     "<div dir=\"ltr\">I fixed the problem by using this code:<div><br></div><div>ggplot(data = watersurf, aes( x = time, y = data))+ geom_line(aes(linetype = group1, colour = group1), size = 0.2) + facet_wrap(~ id)<br></div><div>\r\n<br></div><div>Thank you. </div><div><br></div><div>Best Regards, </div><div>Janesh Devkota</div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Mon, Jan 21, 2013 at 10:09 PM, Janesh Devkota <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">janesh....@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br>\r\n<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.727272033691406px\">Hello All, </span><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.727272033691406px\">\r\n<br></div><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.727272033691406px\">\r\nI am trying to do the comparison of my observed and modeled data sets for two stations. One station is called station &quot;red&quot; and another is called &quot;blue&quot;. I was able to create the facets but when I tried to add two series in one facet then only one facet got updated while other didn&#39;t. </div>\r\n\r\n<div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.727272033691406px\"><br></div><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.727272033691406px\"><p style=\"clear:both;vertical-align:baseline;line-height:17.600000381469727px;font-size:13.600000381469727px;font-family:Arial,&#39;Liberation Sans&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans&#39;,sans-serif;margin:0px 0px 1em;word-wrap:break-word;border:0px;padding:0px\">\r\n\r\n<span style=\"font-size:13.600000381469727px;line-height:17.600000381469727px\">This means for blue only one series is plotted and for red two series are plotted.</span><br></p></div><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.727272033691406px\">\r\n\r\n<br></div><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.727272033691406px\">The data watersurf1.csv can be downloaded from <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ainioj2nn47sis4/watersurf1.csv\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.dropbox.com/s/ainioj2nn47sis4/watersurf1.csv&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792373575105000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0hLzd55GrbwrA3jhB-l_tv\">https://www.dropbox.com/s/ainioj2nn47sis4/watersurf1.csv</a></div>\r\n\r\n<div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.727272033691406px\"><br></div><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.727272033691406px\">The output I got can be found on <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/a6d13bkjiu7uy2q/facet%202%20subplots.png\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.dropbox.com/s/a6d13bkjiu7uy2q/facet%25202%2520subplots.png&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792373575105000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0Omjq_pLZRJ8Wld-sFIUCp\">https://www.dropbox.com/s/a6d13bkjiu7uy2q/facet%202%20subplots.png</a></div>\r\n\r\n<div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.727272033691406px\"><br></div><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.727272033691406px\">The code I used is as follows:</div><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.727272033691406px\">\r\n\r\n<br></div><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.727272033691406px\"><div>watersurf &lt;- read.table(&quot;watersurf1.csv&quot;,sep=&quot;,&quot;,header=TRUE)</div><div>watersurf[1:100,]</div><div>ggplot(data=watersurf,aes(x=time,y=data))+geom_line()+facet_wrap(~id)</div>\r\n\r\n<div><br></div><div>watersurf$coupleid &lt;- factor(rep(unlist(by(watersurf$id,watersurf$group,</div><div>                                           function(x) {ave(as.numeric(unique(x)),FUN=seq_along)}</div><div>                                           )),each=6239))</div>\r\n\r\n<div>                             </div><div>                 </div><div>p &lt;- ggplot(data=watersurf,aes(x=time,y=data,group=id))+geom_line(aes(linetype=group1),size=1)+facet_wrap(~coupleid)</div><div>p</div></div><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.727272033691406px\">\r\n\r\n<br></div><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.727272033691406px\">Is it also possible to add third series in the graph but of unequal length i.e not same interval ? </div><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.727272033691406px\">\r\n\r\n<br></div><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.727272033691406px\"><p style=\"clear:both;vertical-align:baseline;line-height:17.600000381469727px;font-size:13.600000381469727px;font-family:Arial,&#39;Liberation Sans&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans&#39;,sans-serif;margin:0px 0px 1em;word-wrap:break-word;border:0px;padding:0px\">\r\n\r\nI followed the example on this page to create the graphs. <a href=\"http://www.ats.ucla.edu/stat/r/faq/growth.htm\" rel=\"nofollow\" style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;font-size:13.600000381469727px;vertical-align:baseline;background-color:transparent;color:rgb(74,107,130);text-decoration:initial\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.ats.ucla.edu/stat/r/faq/growth.htm&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792373575105000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0kGrokTdKX8Vf6IuGPfcnW\">http://www.ats.ucla.edu/stat/r/faq/growth.htm</a></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"clear:both;vertical-align:baseline;line-height:17.600000381469727px;font-size:13.600000381469727px;font-family:Arial,&#39;Liberation Sans&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans&#39;,sans-serif;margin:0px 0px 1em;word-wrap:break-word;border:0px;padding:0px\">\r\n\r\nThanks.</p><p style=\"clear:both;vertical-align:baseline;line-height:17.600000381469727px;font-size:13.600000381469727px;font-family:Arial,&#39;Liberation Sans&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans&#39;,sans-serif;margin:0px 0px 1em;word-wrap:break-word;border:0px;padding:0px\">\r\n\r\n<span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.727272033691406px;line-height:normal;color:rgb(34,34,34)\">Best Regards, </span><span><font color=\"#888888\"><br></font></span></p></div><span><font color=\"#888888\"><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.727272033691406px\">\r\n\r\nJanesh Devkota</div></font></span></div>\r\n</blockquote></div><br></div>\r\n"
